        tabLabel: 'About',
        pages: [
          {
            title: '52 Pick-up',
            subtitle: 'Card game',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '52 Pick-up is a social prank using a standard 52-card pack. One player offers a game, scatters all the cards over the floor, and the other player is expected to pick them up. The source explicitly notes that it is not really a card game, so this record treats it as a social card-game joke rather than a competitive rules engine target.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '52 Pick-up is a long-standing English-language practical joke played with a standard deck. Reports place the prank before the 1974 novel titled 52 Pick-Up, including memories from the 1940s and later family play.',
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Two people: the prankster who proposes the game and the target who accepts.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'One standard 52-card deck.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'A clear floor or table area where scattered cards can be recovered safely.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'There is no real deal. The prankster scatters the whole pack after the target agrees to play.',
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Variations',
            subtitle: 'Known ways this game changes',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'list',
                style: 'unordered',
                items: [
                  {
                    text: '52 card pickup: Common alternate wording for the same prank.',
                  },
                ],
              },
            ],
          },
